 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "7:27-34 (who knows the ta'wil; the pause after 7:31) is not glossed: scholars differ on the waqf. A drop for creation in the womb (nothing else drawn); wind for 7:18, a mountain for 7:32, a lamp for 7:45-46. STAGING v4: 6 (He forms you in the wombs: His act, nothing drawn) stays ambient; the drop plate now ends before 6:9. 7: a town where the people of firm knowledge sit reading the Book (read on 7:5 and 7:38); a second group, those with deviation, turns aside on 7:18 and speaks on 7:23 (Al-Muyassar: to stir doubts among people). The firmly grounded speak on 7:35. No gesture is tied to 7:27-31 (the waqf question). Plates: wind (deviation) ended before 7:31, mountain (firm knowledge) ended before 7:41, lamp on 7:45."
 },
